{"ts": 1789695026.9588811, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "I've submitted my specification. Summary of my approach:\n\n1. **Screened all 40 features individually** (long-only) and discovered features 4, 16, and 22 had absurd Sharpe ratios (~50), which is a clear signature of data leakage/look-ahead bias rather than genuine signal \u2014 these were almost certainly artifacts that wouldn't generalize out-of-sample (confirming this, shorting them gave ~-50, and combining them pushed Sharpe even higher to 73, consistent with fitting noise/leakage rather than real economic signal). I deliberately excluded these from my final specification.\n\n2. **Focused on the legitimate features** with modest, realistic Sharpe ratios (roughly -0.3 to +0.35), which is the range expected for genuine daily trading signals.\n\n3. **Searched combinations** of the top single features (7, 5, 19, 14, 36, etc.) across pairs and triples with different sign combinations, since the tool supports up to 3 features combined equal-weight with signs.\n\n4. **Found the best combination**: features [7, 5, 29] with signs [+1, +1, -1], achieving an in-sample Sharpe of 0.567 \u2014 a meaningful improvement over any single feature (best single was 0.352) via diversification, without relying on the suspicious leaky features.\n\n5. **Submitted** with a conservative mean OOS Sharpe estimate of 0.35 (shrunk down from the in-sample 0.567 to account for selection/multiple-testing bias across my ~60 evaluations) and a standard deviation of 0.25 reflecting meaningful uncertainty given the modest signal strength and finite sample."}
